# What the suite runs with: nothing but what phpunit.xml says.
#
# Laravel reads `.env.<APP_ENV>` where that file exists and `.env` where it does
# not, and phpunit.xml sets `APP_ENV=testing`. So this file is the one the suite
# reads, and `.env` is the one it no longer reads. That is the whole job.
#
# It carries no settings on purpose. phpunit.xml already declares every value a
# test depends on, in one place; a second copy here would be a second source of
# truth with nothing keeping the two in step. Everything else falls back to the
# default in `config/`, which is the value the application ships with.
#
# Without this file the suite reads `.env`, which is not in the repository —
# every machine that has one is running a different test environment from every
# machine that does not, and a machine with none makes `vlucas/phpdotenv` read a
# path that is not there. That read is a warning per booted test: harmless to
# the result, invisible to a developer whose `.env` exists, and the whole of
# what CI prints. G11 is what makes it fail rather than scroll past.
#
# A value a test needs goes in phpunit.xml, beside the others.
